(My business idea is Morning Cup, a proposed tea stall serving office workers in) Tj T*
(Hinjawadi Phase 1, Pune, Maharashtra, India.) Tj T*
(I have not started regular operations.) Tj T*
(Workers have short morning breaks and sometimes wait in queues for tea.) Tj T*
(I would offer tea with pre-order pickup and reusable-cup discounts.) Tj T*
(I spoke to 30 workers: 18 would consider buying, 8 preferred existing stalls and 4 were) Tj T*
(unsure.) Tj T*
(There are no confirmed orders or advance payments.) Tj T*
(Three existing tea stalls serve the area at similar prices.) Tj T*
(My proposed difference is scheduled pickup, but customers have not yet tested it or) Tj T*
(confirmed that they value it.) Tj T*
(I can prepare tea and handle payments, and plan to hire one helper.) Tj T*
(I need tea leaves, milk, sugar, drinking water and paper cups.) Tj T*
(A local dairy and wholesale grocery shop are potential suppliers, but prices and supply) Tj T*
(agreements are not confirmed.) Tj T*
(Startup investment is INR 60000 for equipment, a deposit and opening stock.) Tj T*
(Own funds are INR 20000 and requested loan is INR 25000.) Tj T*
(The loan is not approved and I have no other funding committed.) Tj T*
(The selling price is INR 20 per cup.) Tj T*
(I estimate selling 60 cups per day for 25 operating days per month.) Tj T*
(Estimated revenue is INR 30000 per month.) Tj T*
(Variable cost is INR 8 per cup, or INR 12000 per month at these sales.) Tj T*
(Monthly fixed costs are rent INR 10000, helper wages INR 7000, transport INR 3000 and) Tj T*
(utilities INR 2000.) Tj T*
(Total expenses are INR 34000 per month, giving an estimated operating loss of INR 4000) Tj T*
(per month before tax and borrowing costs.) Tj T*
(I have not confirmed site permission, loan terms or food-business registration.) Tj T*
(I want mentoring to test customer demand, secure permission and funding, and revise the) Tj T*
(cost and sales plan before opening.) Tj T*
